  "_what": "Every PREDEFINED IAM role that reads log entries project-wide, as measured on the date below. A role is here when its includedPermissions carry at least one of the three permissions Cloud Logging entries.list accepts: logging.logEntries.list, logging.privateLogEntries.list, logging.views.access. The value is which of the three it carries.",
  "_how": "GET https://iam.googleapis.com/v1/roles?view=FULL&pageSize=1000, all pages, read-only: 2397 predefined roles. 15 returned no permission list (13 BETA roles, plus roles/gkebackup.crossProjectServiceAgent and roles/spanner.databaseRoleUser), none of them a logging role, and are not judged here. Read by terraform/bootstrap/verify_logs.tf (local.log_reading_roles; var.deployer_roles refuses every role here) and tests/terraform/verify_logs.tftest.hcl.",
  "_limits": "A DENYLIST MEASURED ON A DATE. Google adds roles and adds permissions to existing ones, so a role absent here may read logs later. local.deployer_roles_reviewed in verify_logs.tf is what refuses a role nobody has weighed; this file is what refuses a known reader even if someone marks it reviewed.",
